{
    desc => 'ciw changes inner word and enters insert mode',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/text_object_ciw`

Tests the `ciw` text object which deletes the word under the cursor
and enters insert mode, then we type replacement text.

**initial.png** — Cursor on 'h' of `hello` at line 1 col 0.

Keys: `ciw` then type `HI` then `<Escape>`

**after_ciw.png** — The word `hello` is replaced with `HI`.
Line 1 now reads `HI   world   this`. Cursor in normal mode on the 'I'.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('ciw');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->type('HI');
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_ciw');
    },
}
__DATA__
hello   world   this
